# Build-Time Validation

Documentation breaks quietly when a page moves and old links keep shipping. CarvePress makes those failures explicit.

The build validates internal links, nav items, sidebar items, `prev` and `next` frontmatter overrides, and Carve cross-references. The GitHub Pages workflow for this repo runs the docs build on pull requests without deploying them, so broken docs fail the check before publication.

See [Writing Content](/guide/writing-content) for the author-facing rules.
